CI correction after native Windows run 35046857944.

The Windows backend compiled and then failed five voice installation/removal tests. The shared root cause was the Silero catalog revision `sha256:<digest>` being used directly as a directory name; `:` is illegal in Windows path components.

Fix:
- Catalog revision validation is now the single authority for the portable directory component.
- Commit revisions keep their 40-hex directory name.
- sha256 revisions retain the exact `sha256:<digest>` value in receipts but use only the 64-hex digest on disk.
- Installation, receipt lookup, and startup cleanup all use that same normalized component.
- Invalid receipt revisions remain rejected and resolve only to a closed fallback path if constructed outside the loader.

Validation:
- Voice download tests: 36 passed
- cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings: green
- git diff --check: green
- graphify update .: completed
- Native Windows run 35046857944 proved compilation and exposed the five path failures after 5562 passing tests.
